    "https://recruiting.myapps.paychex.com/appone/MainInfoReq.asp?R_ID=7193968&B_ID=91&fid=1&Adid=&SearchScreenID=26243&CountryID=3&LanguageID=2": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Nursing, Medical- Surgical and NCLEX Success Coach",
      "description": "Job Information: Assistant Professor of Nursing, Medical- Surgical and NCLEX Success Coach Job Share Email Opening Apply Now Title Assistant Professor of Nursing, Medical- Surgical and NCLEX Success Coach EOE Statement We are an equal employment opportunity employer.  All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to any category protected by applicable federal, state or local law, including but not limited to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, physical or mental disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, uniformed service member status or any other characteristic protected by law. About the Organization Saint Vincent College is an educational community rooted in the tradition of the Catholic faith, the heritage of Benedictine monasticism, and the love of values inherent in the liberal approach to life and learning. Our mission is to provide quality undergraduate and graduate education for men and women to enable them to integrate their professional aims with the broader purposes of human life. The programs, activities, and encounters that make up student life at Saint Vincent College encourages the intellectual gifts, professional aptitudes and personal aspirations of students to mature harmoniously. Position Assistant Professor of Nursing, Medical- Surgical and NCLEX Success Coach Location Saint Vincent College Full-Time/Part-Time Full-Time Shift -not applicable- Exempt/Non-Exempt Exempt Description Position Title : Assistant Professor of Nursing, Medical- Surgical and NCLEX Success Coach Reports to: Chairperson, Department of Nursing Supervises: N/A Primary function: The Saint Vincent College Department of Nursing is seeking a full-time faculty member with expertise in Medical-Surgical Nursing. The successful candidate will contribute to the academic mission of the department through high-quality teaching, student mentorship, curriculum development, and scholarly engagement. This role is ideal for a nurse educator who is passionate about preparing the next generation of professional nurses and advancing excellence in medical-surgical practice. This position will be pivotal in the ongoing development and implementation of the nursing program. The faculty member will work closely with other faculty, staff, and external partners to ensure compliance with the Essentials: Core Competencies for Professional Nursing Education and accreditation standards in the delivery of baccalaureate and master’s level education, support of grant-funded projects, and advance the mission and strategic goals of the nursing program and Saint Vincent College. The faculty member will report directly to the Chair of the Department of Nursing and lead a coordinated, data-driven NCLEX success strategy by overseeing ATI integration, standardizing testing and remediation processes, training faculty, and delivering targeted NCLEX preparation. This is a 12-month position with faculty rank appropriate for qualifications and previous experience that maintains teaching responsibilities each semester through the calendar year. Candidates with a doctoral degree are eligible for a tenure-track appointment. Required Qualifications: Current (unencumbered) license as a Registered Nurse and/or APRN in the state of Pennsylvania. National certification upon hire or within 2 years of eligibility. Demonstrated ability to teach effectively at the college or university level (classroom, clinical, and/or simulation). Proven leadership skills with demonstrated ability to manage projects and advise students and faculty. Exceptional organizational ability with great attention to detail. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Preferred Experience with curriculum development, simulation pedagogy, and/or innovative teaching strategies. Evidence of scholarly productivity or potential for research. Familiarity with accreditation standards (e.g., CCNE) and program assessment. Experience with NCLEX success program (e.g., ATI). Education: An earned doctorate in nursing or current enrollment in a doctoral program is required. Experience: Minimum of 5 years of experience in clinical nursing practice. A minimum of 3 years of teaching experience in an academic setting or healthcare institution working with clinical disciplines (nursing, medicine, pharmacy, and/or other health-related fields, etc.). Key Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate and/or graduate nursing courses with a primary focus on medical-surgical nursing and associated courses such as population health, vulnerable populations, and community health in classroom, clinical, and simulation settings. Develop and revise curriculum to ensure alignment with current evidence-based practice, accreditation standards, and program outcomes. Supervise and evaluate students in clinical placements, skills labs, and simulation experiences. Function as ATI champion. Coordinate ATI integration across the curriculum to optimize student subscriptions and resource utilization Design and deliver faculty orientation and ongoing training on ATI tools, testing processes, and best practices Define and standardize student practice, remediation, and testing workflows to ensure consistency and accountability Define and standardize student practice, remediation, and testing processes Coordinate NCLEX preparation courses for senior BSN and Year 2 DE-MSN students Monitor student performance data to identify trends, intervene early, and support at-risk students Collaborate with faculty to align NCLEX readiness strategies with curricular outcomes and accreditation requirements. Provide individualized coaching for at-risk students Develop structured remediation plans Support students’ transition from coursework to licensure preparation Advise and mentor students, supporting academic success, professional development, and progression through the program. Engage in scholarly activities, which may include research, publications, presentations, or practice-based inquiry. Participate in departmental and institutional service, including committee work, program assessment, and accreditation activities. Maintain active professional practice or continuing education to stay current in the field of medical-surgical nursing. Collaborate with other departments within Saint Vincent College to facilitate interprofessional education and collaborative teaching/learning/research opportunities. Other Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Extensive knowledge of nursing pedagogy, program operations, standards of best practice and instructional techniques/technologies. 2. Knowledge and experience of curriculum design and implementation. 3. Strong interpersonal, communication, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, staff, students, and external partners. 4. Ability to foster a culture of respect, collaboration, innovation, and continuous quality improvement. 5. Ability to lift and move lab equipment, mannequins, and other training models. Special challenges and environment: Saint Vincent College is a Catholic, Benedictine liberal arts and sciences college of about 1400 undergraduate students and 200 graduate students. Located in Latrobe, Pennsylvania and the beautiful Laurel highlands, Saint Vincent College offers rich opportunities with an infrastructure that provides the foundation for scholarly success. Saint Vincent Nursing is a collaborative team that partners on education, creates innovative clinical experiences, and shares a vision for the future of healthcare in this country. Nursing faculty will be located in our new state-of-the-art building that houses the Center for Excellence and Innovation in Nursing and that includes the nursing skills lab, simulation lab, and immersive learning spaces. A career with Saint Vincent College will provide you with an exciting opportunity to help set a path for educating the future generations of nurses! All positions require the incumbent to be able to fully embrace the unique mission and identity of the College as a Catholic, Benedictine liberal arts and sciences institution. Saint Vincent College is committed to diversity and encourages applicants from all qualified candidates. Saint Vincent College is committed to building a diversified and competent population of faculty and staff, and encourages applications from women and minorities. Saint Vincent is an equal opportunity employer. PLEASE NOTE: Background checks will be performed on all new hires. Employment is conditional upon satisfactory background checks and clearances. This description is not intended to be all-inclusive. It is provided as a general statement of the nature and duties of the position. The incumbent may be asked to perform other assignments of a similar nature, or related to the effective operation of the department, or as a developmental experience, as assigned from time to time by the supervisor. Tags position, shift, city, state This position is currently accepting applications. Apply Now WE ALSO RECOMMEND Other Jobs Within Same Category Assistant Professor of Nursing, Medical-Surgical Clinical Placement Coordinator in Latrobe, PA Posted on: 7/2/2026 [Apply Now] Assistant Professor of Computing and Information Systems in Latrobe, PA Posted on: 10/21/2025 [Apply Now] Other Jobs Within 60 Miles Administrative Human Resource Associate in Latrobe, PA Posted on: 8/31/2026 [Apply Now] Head Coach: Women’s Rugby in Latrobe, PA Posted on: 7/24/2026 [Apply Now] Head Coach: Men's Rugby in Latrobe, PA Posted on: 7/24/2026 [Apply Now] Accounting Assistant in Latrobe, PA Posted on: 8/10/2026 [Apply Now] Accounting & Finance Manager in Latrobe, PA Posted on: 8/10/2026 [Apply Now] Follow us See who works here: App One .com TM ©1999-2024 HR Services, Inc. Click here for technical assistance. We use cookies and other technologies to support site functionality, analytics, preferences, marketing, and to improve your experience and our services.\r\n        We use third party technologies that may access your information. By continuing to use our site, you expressly consent to such use.\r\n        For more information, see our Privacy Policy. Continue We use cookies and other technologies to support site functionality, analytics, preferences, and to improve your experience and our services. We use third party technologies that may access your information.\r\n\t        By continuing to use our site, you expressly consent to such use. For more information, see our Privacy Policy. Continue"
