 research, publications, presentations, or practice-based inquiry. Participate in departmental and institutional service, including committee work, program assessment, and accreditation activities. Maintain active professional practice or continuing education to stay current in the field of medical-surgical nursing. Collaborate with other departments within Saint Vincent College to facilitate interprofessional education and collaborative teaching/learning/research opportunities. Other Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Extensive knowledge of nursing pedagogy, program operations, standards of best practice and instructional techniques/technologies. 2. Knowledge and experience of curriculum design and implementation. 3. Strong interpersonal, communication, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, staff, students, and external partners. 4. Ability to foster a culture of respect, collaboration, innovation, and continuous quality improvement. 5. Ability to lift and move lab equipment, mannequins, and other training models. Special challenges and environment: Saint Vincent College is a Catholic, Benedictine liberal arts and sciences college of about 1400 undergraduate students and 200 graduate students. Located in Latrobe, Pennsylvania and the beautiful Laurel highlands, Saint Vincent College offers rich opportunities with an infrastructure that provides the foundation for scholarly success. Saint Vincent Nursing is a collaborative team that partners on education, creates innovative clinical experiences, and shares a vision for the future of healthcare in this country. Nursing faculty will be located in our new state-of-the-art building that houses the Center for Excellence and Innovation in Nursing and that includes the nursing skills lab, simulation lab, and immersive learning spaces. A career with Saint Vincent College will provide you with an exciting opportunity to help set a path for educating the future generations of nurses! All positions require the incumbent to be able to fully embrace the unique mission and identity of the College as a Catholic, Benedictine liberal arts and sciences institution. Saint Vincent College is committed to diversity and encourages applicants from all qualified candidates. Saint Vincent College is committed to building a diversified and competent population of faculty and staff, and encourages applications from women and minorities. Saint Vincent is an equal opportunity employer. PLEASE NOTE: Background checks will be performed on all new hires. Employment is conditional upon satisfactory background checks and clearances. This description is not intended to be all-inclusive. It is provided as a general statement of the nature and duties of the position. The incumbent may be asked to perform other assignments of a similar nature, or related to the effective operation of the department, or as a developmental experience, as assigned from time to time by the supervisor. Tags position, shift, city, state This position is currently accepting applications. Apply Now WE ALSO RECOMMEND Other Jobs Within Same Category Assistant Professor of Nursing, Medical- Surgical and NCLEX Success Coach in Latrobe, PA Posted on: 7/20/2026 [Apply Now] Assistant Professor of Computing and Information Systems in Latrobe, PA Posted on: 10/21/2025 [Apply Now] Other Jobs Within 60 Miles Administrative Human Resource Associate in Latrobe, PA Posted on: 8/31/2026 [Apply Now] Head Coach: Women’s Rugby in Latrobe, PA Posted on: 7/24/2026 [Apply Now] Head Coach: Men's Rugby in Latrobe, PA Posted on: 7/24/2026 [Apply Now] Accounting Assistant in Latrobe, PA Posted on: 8/10/2026 [Apply Now] Accounting & Finance Manager in Latrobe, PA Posted on: 8/10/2026 [Apply Now] Follow us See who works here: App One .com TM ©1999-2024 HR Services, Inc. Click here for technical assistance. We use cookies and other technologies to support site functionality, analytics, preferences, marketing, and to 